`src/cli.js` now implements `merge`, `merge2` and `regions`, and `node --test test/*.test.js` passes all 15 visible tests.

I didn't run anything beyond that suite, so the corners the visible tests don't pin down are untested. That includes the held-back cases the validator will run, which cover:
- the exit codes;
- the two error messages;
- how a region with changes from both sides gets its replacement lines;
- empty documents.

The whole program is in that one file; I didn't split it across other files under `src/`.

I made one reading call on `regions` output. It prints a `stable N` line only for a stretch of base lines that isn't empty, so two adjacent regions get no zero-length `stable 0` line between them.

I didn't touch `test/` or `package.json`, and added no dependencies.

